# Root-anchored above, which misses the one that actually gets written: the
# SDG Hub flow is downloaded at runtime beside the pipeline, not at the root,
# and its prompt copy shadows the asset under assets/sdghub/. Editing the
# download has no effect and raises no error, so keep it out of the tree.
workflows/examples/code_understanding/flows/

# Local tooling artifacts
.coverage
htmlcov/
mlflow.db
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Written into the working directory by the indexing tests
indexing_result_*.json

# Planning and session scratch. This repository keeps these local rather than
# tracked: they carry per-session context for one contributor's workflow and
# would read as noise in a shared history. Anything worth keeping goes in a
# commit message or in documentation for the code it describes.
NEXT_SESSION*.md
EPICS.md
session-summaries/
PROMPT_ANALYSIS*.md

# Agent instructions for this checkout. Local for the same reason: it encodes
# one contributor's working conventions, and a shared repository should not
# inherit them without the other maintainers agreeing to them first. Rooted so
# a tracked CLAUDE.md can still be added under a subdirectory later.
/CLAUDE.md

# GraphRAG copies the prompts it runs with into a prompts/ directory beside the
# index. The tracked source of truth is assets/graphrag/.
workflows/examples/code_understanding/prompts/
